# Test Org-Scoped Admin Model
# This file demonstrates the organization-scoped admin functionality

### Step 1: Register Organization A
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/registration
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "OrgA Admin",
  "email": "admin-orga@flocci.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+1234567890",
  "role": "ORGANIZATION"
}

### Step 2: Create Organization A
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orgA_token}}

{
  "orgName": "Tech Solutions Inc",
  "sector": "Technology",
  "licenseId": "TECH001",
  "contactInfo": {
    "address": "123 Tech Street",
    "city": "San Francisco"
  }
}

### Step 3: Register Organization B
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/registration
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "OrgB Admin", 
  "email": "admin-orgb@flocci.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+1234567891",
  "role": "ORGANIZATION"
}

### Step 4: Create Organization B
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orgB_token}}

{
  "orgName": "Healthcare Partners LLC",
  "sector": "Healthcare",
  "licenseId": "HEALTH001",
  "contactInfo": {
    "address": "456 Medical Blvd",
    "city": "Boston"
  }
}

### Step 5: Register Consumer
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/registration
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Consumer",
  "email": "consumer@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+1234567892",
  "role": "CONSUMER"
}

### Step 6: Consumer Login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "consumer@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Step 7: Consumer submits testimony about Organization A
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/testimonies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{consumer_token}}

{
  "subjectId": "{{orgA_userId}}",
  "content": "Excellent tech support and innovative solutions!",
  "category": "SERVICE_QUALITY"
}

### Step 8: Consumer submits testimony about Organization B  
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/testimonies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{consumer_token}}

{
  "subjectId": "{{orgB_userId}}",
  "content": "Outstanding healthcare services and caring staff!",
  "category": "SERVICE_QUALITY"
}

### === ORG-SCOPED ADMIN TESTING ===

### Step 9: OrgA Admin Login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin-orga@flocci.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Step 10: OrgA Admin - View Dashboard Stats (should only see OrgA data)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/admin/dashboard/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{orgA_admin_token}}

### Step 11: OrgA Admin - Get Pending Testimonies (should only see testimonies about OrgA)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/admin/testimonies/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{orgA_admin_token}}

### Step 12: OrgB Admin Login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin-orgb@flocci.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Step 13: OrgB Admin - Get Pending Testimonies (should only see testimonies about OrgB)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/admin/testimonies/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{orgB_admin_token}}

### Step 14: OrgA Admin - Try to verify testimony about OrgA (should work)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/admin/verifications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orgA_admin_token}}

{
  "testimonyId": "{{orgA_testimony_id}}",
  "outcome": "VERIFIED",
  "notes": "Verified by OrgA admin"
}

### Step 15: OrgA Admin - Try to verify testimony about OrgB (should fail with authorization error)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/api/v1/admin/verifications  
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orgA_admin_token}}

{
  "testimonyId": "{{orgB_testimony_id}}",
  "outcome": "VERIFIED", 
  "notes": "Attempt to verify other org's testimony"
}